            <p>London Heathrow processed over 79 million passengers annually before pandemic disruptions, ranking as Europe's busiest airport and one of the world's most significant aviation nodes. Its five terminals and extensive long-haul network make it the natural destination for Pittsburgh's transatlantic ambitions.</p>
            <h2>Airlines Flying from Pittsburgh to London</h2>
            <p>A competitive field serves this corridor, with seasonal nonstop operations complementing year-round connecting alternatives through major hubs.</p>

            <h3>Full-Service Carriers</h3>

            <h3>British Airways</h3>

            <p>British Airways operates the only nonstop service on this route, leveraging its oneworld alliance strength and Pittsburgh's strategic importance.</p>

            <p><b>Signature elements:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Seasonal nonstop service from PIT to London Heathrow, typically operating May through October</li>
                <li>Boeing 787-8 Dreamliner deployment, offering improved cabin pressure and fuel efficiency</li>
                <li>Multiple weekly frequencies during peak summer months</li>
                <li>Executive Club Avios earning with extensive partner redemption possibilities</li>
                <li>Club World business class featuring lie-flat seats and British dining</li>
                <li>Strong connections throughout the UK, Europe, Africa, and Asia beyond London</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>American Airlines</h3>

            <p>American competes through its oneworld partnership with British Airways and its Philadelphia and Charlotte hubs.</p>

            <p><b>Key characteristics:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Connections through Philadelphia (PHL) and Charlotte (CLT) with excellent onward timing</li>
                <li>AAdvantage program earning with reciprocal benefits on British Airways</li>
                <li>Flagship Business class on transatlantic segments</li>
                <li>Strong Pittsburgh market presence through regional feeder operations</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Delta Air Lines</h3>

            <p>Delta routes Pittsburgh passengers through its Atlanta and New York hubs.</p>

            <p><b>Notable features:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Connections through Atlanta (ATL) and New York-JFK with well-timed onward segments</li>
                <li>SkyMiles earning with Air France/KLM/Alitalia partnerships</li>
                <li>Delta One suites on premium transatlantic routes</li>
                <li>Strong domestic network from Pittsburgh</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>United Airlines</h3>

            <p>United competes through its Newark hub and Star Alliance partnerships.</p>
            <p><b>Distinctive positioning:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Connections through Newark (EWR) and Chicago O'Hare (ORD)</li>
                <li>MileagePlus earning with Lufthansa/Austrian/Swiss partnerships</li>
                <li>Polaris business class on long-haul segments</li>
                <li>Strong Pittsburgh-Newark shuttle service facilitating connections</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Virgin Atlantic</h3>

            <p>Virgin Atlantic offers an alternative British flavor through its Delta partnership.</p>
            <p><b>Appeal:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Connections through Atlanta and New York-JFK</li>
                <li>Distinctive onboard service and entertainment</li>
                <li>Flying Club earning with Delta SkyMiles reciprocity</li>
                <li>Upper Class premium cabin with onboard bar</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>JetBlue Airways</h3>

            <p>JetBlue has expanded its transatlantic presence through London service.</p>
            <p><b>Profile:</b></p>
