            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>Q1: Are there direct flights from Pittsburgh to London?</h3>

            <p>British Airways operates seasonal nonstop service from May through October, typically 3-5 times weekly. Winter travel requires connections through Philadelphia, Newark, Chicago, Atlanta, or New York.</p>

            <h3>Q2: What is the cheapest time to fly from Pittsburgh to London?</h3>

            <p>January and February offer the lowest fares, with economy round-trips often available at $500-$850. Summer months command premium pricing. Book 45-60 days ahead for best peak-season rates.</p>

            <h3>Q3: Do US citizens need a visa for the UK?</h3>

            <p>No visa required for tourism or business stays under six months. A valid passport with six months of remaining validity suffices—no additional documentation needed for standard visits.</p>

            <h3>Q4: Which airline offers the best connection from Pittsburgh to London?</h3>

            <p>American Airlines through Philadelphia provides the most convenient connection with the shortest total journey time. British Airways seasonal nonstop offers ultimate convenience. Icelandair through Reykjavik often provides the lowest total fare.</p>

            <h3>Q5: How do I get from Heathrow airport to central London?</h3>

            <p>Heathrow Express reaches Paddington in 15 minutes for approximately £25. The Elizabeth Line connects to central London in 35-40 minutes for £12-£15. The Tube takes 45-60 minutes for approximately £6. Taxis cost £50-£80.</p>

            <h3>Q6: Can I use US dollars in London?</h3>

            <p>The pound sterling (£) is the UK's currency. US dollars are not accepted. Credit cards work universally; contactless payment preferred. ATMs plentiful throughout the city. Notify your bank before travel.</p>

            <h3>Q7: What should I pack for London?</h3>

            <p>Comfortable walking shoes essential for cobblestones and museum marathons. Layers for unpredictable weather. Waterproof jacket. Smart casual attire for theater and dining—universal power adapter for UK outlets (Type G).</p>

            <h3>Q8: Is London safe for American tourists?</h3>

            <p>London is generally safe with standard urban precautions. Pickpockets operate in tourist zones and on the Tube. Violent crime against tourists is rare. Police presence visible. Emergency number is 999.</p>

            <h3>Q9: What is the best way to avoid jet lag flying Pittsburgh to London?</h3>

            <p>Choose evening departures arriving in London in the morning. Sleep on the flight. Upon arrival, expose yourself to daylight immediately, stay active until local evening, and avoid heavy meals. Hydration throughout the journey is essential.</p>

            <h3>Q10: Can I visit other UK cities from London easily?</h3>

            <p>Yes. Trains connect London to Edinburgh (4.5 hours), Manchester (2 hours), and Bath (1.5 hours). Budget airlines serve regional airports. Rental cars are available, but driving in London challenging. Consider open-jaw tickets.</p>


